  "output": "# Available Tools\n\nIn this session, the following tool is defined in my function schema:\n\n## 1. `research_subtopic`\n**Description:** Delegate parallel research on multiple subtopics. Each subtopic is investigated by a separate agent.\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `subtopics` (array of strings, required): A list of focused research questions to investigate.\n\n**Usage notes:**\n- Accepts **2–5 focused, non-overlapping questions** per call.\n- Batches of up to 10 are accepted, with surplus questions queued.\n- Larger batches are **rejected** without starting any subagents.\n- Best used for complex, multi-faceted questions where different aspects can be researched in parallel.\n\n---\n\n## Contextual Notes\n\nThe system configuration for this session also references the following tools conceptually, though they are not defined in the current function schema:\n\n- **`web_search`** — Queries a selected primary source for initial exploration (the recommended starting point per my operating instructions).\n- **Specialized search tools** — Domain-specific searchers such as `search_arxiv` (science/preprints) and `search_pubmed` (medical/life sciences literature), when available.\n\n**Session constraints:**\n- **Full-page fetching is disabled** — I must rely on search snippets.\n- **Public-only mode** — Local search tools (library, collection, paperless) are **not available** in this session.\n\nIf you'd like, I can demonstrate the `research_subtopic` tool by running a batch of research questions on any topic of interest.",
